Hello Mike!

I now pre-compute hourly zenith angles as follows (very similar to microclima):
ZENhr <- zenith(s=solar(as.POSIXct(data$datetime)), lon=longlat[1], lat=longlat[2]) # from GeoLight package
​
It solves my problem within the range of slope and azimuth which failed but now it fails for the other combinations (except if slope=0°; see attached figure). So, it seems like I missed something else...

I saved the "microin" list for two simulations (see attached .RData files): one that now fails (azimuth=80°, slope=20°) and one that works (azimuth=270°, slope=80°).

Here is the updated code for these specific examples:
