Hello everyone,

I'm a master's student interested in using DEB theory with NicheMapR. I cannot understand how to calculate the thermal response parameters: Arrhenius lower boundary (T_L),  Arrhenius upper boundary (T_H) and their respective Arrhenius temperatures (TAL, TAH).

I would like to determine the parameters for the anchovy Engraulis japonicus. From what I understand, all the data I need are already available <https://www.bio.vu.nl/thb/deb/deblab/add_my_pet/entries_web/Engraulis_japonicus/Engraulis_japonicus_res.html>: the Arrhenius temperature T_A and univariate data detailing rates at various temperatures. However, when I run the "run_my_species.m" file I do not get any temperature parameters output in the "results.mat" file. I have also searched for a DEBtool routine but could not find one.

I have read the DEBvignette, DEBtool manual and AmP Estimation pages. I see these parameters mentioned but no explanation of how they're calculated. I feel like I'm missing something obvious - any help or advice would be greatly appreciated.

Best regards,

Neil Waters

